Vikram and Betal: The Broken Promise (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100133

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a man who made many promises,” said Betal. “But he never kept them.”

One day, he promised his friend that he would help him with some work.

But when the time came, he did not show up.

His friend felt hurt.

Later, the man needed help from the same friend.

He went to him and asked for help.

But the friend said, “You did not keep your promise. Why should I trust you now?”

The man felt sorry and realized his mistake.

He decided to always keep his promises from that day on.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why is keeping promises important?”

Vikram replied, “Because trust is built on keeping promises.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Always keep your promises.
